  "body": "The heavy lane (release, `--ignored`) is red on `main`. The batch tier does not show it: the test has `#[ignore]` and runs only in the heavy lane and in the gate of a cut. The gate of the next cut will fail on it.\n\n## What fails\n\n`camcraft-app`, test binary `pocket3d_hsm`, test `the_users_bore_roughs_adaptive_level_by_level_and_verifies_clean`.\n\n- On Windows, on `main` at `ee91ac3e5` with no other change, the test gives the counts (3158, 3130, 1141).\n- The pinned Windows counts are (4716, 4688, 549).\n- The new counts are equal to the macOS values that the test pins for #2371.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- The takeover run of PR #2678 ran 18 selected heavy steps. 17 passed. This step failed with the same counts on `main` without the PR.\n- The second review of PR #2927 (2026-11-20) made the same note for the Linux pin: the pin of this test was stale after PR #2904, and the heavy lane was red with no issue.\n\n## Cause, as far as known\n\nThe STEP reader and the machining mesh changed on 2026-11-20 (PR #2904, PR #2934, PR #2994). The mesh of the user's bore model is different, so the adaptive passes have other counts. Not known: which of the three PRs moved the counts, and why the Windows counts are now equal to the macOS counts.\n\n## Done when\n\n- The cause is named: the commit that moved the counts, and why.\n- The test verifies clean, and its pins have the correct counts for each platform, with the reason for each change in a decision file. A pin is not changed only to make the test pass: the work first shows that the new toolpath is correct (the verification of the test stays).\n- `cargo xtask gate release --only \"app heavy: pocket3d_hsm\"` is green on Windows.\n\nRefs #2371, #2904, #2934\n",
